    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d240">

                <pb facs="0352" n="246" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg246"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Mr.
                            Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic">November 30, 1891</hi>.</date>
                        (Received January 13, 1892.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 241.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to send herewith copy of
                    communication from Capt. Schley, of the <hi rendition="#italic">Baltimore</hi>,
                    dated 24th instant, with attached correspondence between him and the intendente
                    of Valparaiso up to that date, in relation to the attack upon the men of his
                    ship in Valparaiso on 16th October.</p>
                <p>As will be seen from the correspondence, the men of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Baltimore</hi> appeared before the judge of the court of crimes and gave
                    their evidence on 20th instant, under the conditions approved by the Navy
                    Department.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Patrick Egan</hi>.</signed></closer>







